1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,365
Most AI coding tools pull the project into the agent.

2
00:00:04,365 --> 00:00:20,814
Patchwork flips that model: it lets the Codex session you already have work directly inside the web application, with no embedded chatbot, API key, extension, or separate MCP server.

3
00:00:20,814 --> 00:00:31,835
The human keeps a real local-first workspace: virtual files, a text editor, live preview, checkpoints, and ZIP export.

4
00:00:31,835 --> 00:00:37,977
Everything persists in this browser, and the interface still works when Site Tools are unavailable.

5
00:00:37,977 --> 00:00:46,407
When opened in ChatGPT's built-in browser, Patchwork registers ten WebMCP tools from the top-level document.

6
00:00:46,407 --> 00:00:54,749
This labeled walkthrough invokes those same registered handlers to read only the explicit files needed. Reads do not change the revision.

7
00:00:54,749 --> 00:01:00,671
For the transformation, one bounded multi-file write includes the observed revision.

8
00:01:00,671 --> 00:01:09,733
Patchwork validates every path and size before changing anything, creates a pre-edit checkpoint, commits the batch atomically, and increments the revision once.

9
00:01:09,733 --> 00:01:16,338
The editor and preview update from that same authoritative workspace.

10
00:01:16,338 --> 00:01:22,241
If any item were invalid, the entire batch would be rejected without a partial write.

11
00:01:22,241 --> 00:01:27,628
The walkthrough then inspects the compiler and runtime signals available from the preview.

12
00:01:27,628 --> 00:01:31,979
This run reports no blocking error, so Patchwork makes no invented visual claim.

13
00:01:31,979 --> 00:01:35,764
Every mutation remains recoverable through an explicit checkpoint, and project data never goes to a Patchwork backend.

14
00:01:35,764 --> 00:01:45,228
Patchwork makes WebMCP the structured collaboration layer between a real product interface and the agent the user already has.

15
00:01:45,228 --> 00:01:50,158
Try the live demo and inspect the complete open-source implementation.
